course: dictionary
lesson: 14275
title: Noisome: not about noise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look like they belong to a family you already know. Noisome looks like noise, but it has nothing to do with sound. Do not guess from the shape of a word. Read the clues around it. «The dungeon was dark, damp and noisome.» Dark, damp, and a place no one wants to visit all point to something horrible.
explain: «The sewer was so noisome that the workers held their noses.» Holding your nose is a clue. People do that when something smells very bad. So noisome must mean having a very nasty smell. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Noisome is a formal, literary word. Writers use it in stories to make a place feel disgusting, like a dungeon, a sewer or a rubbish tip. In old books it can also mean harmful or very unpleasant. In the Bible (Psalm 91), God protects people from «the noisome pestilence», a harmful disease.
fact: Noisome means having a very nasty smell.
fact: Noisome is a literary word, found mostly in old books and stories.
fact: Noisome is not connected to noise, even though it looks like it.
fact: In an older sense, noisome means harmful or very unpleasant, as in «the noisome pestilence».
fact: Noisome is an adjective. Its forms are more noisome and most noisome.
exercise: «The sewer was so noisome that nobody wanted to go near it.» What does noisome mean? | *Having a very nasty smell | Very loud, like a noise | Cold and icy | Bright and shiny
exercise: Why should you not guess that noisome means loud? | Because it means quiet and calm | Because it means happy and cheerful | *Because it describes a nasty smell, not sound | Because it sounds like noise, so it must be loud
exercise: «The noisome dungeon made the prisoners feel sick.» Find and copy one clue that shows the dungeon is nasty. | It has a tall window | The dungeon is very big | The prisoners feel sick | *The prisoners feel sick is a clue, so pick the clue that shows the smell
test: «Ancient books describe a noisome swamp.» What does noisome describe? | A swamp that is very cold | A swamp full of bright flowers | *A swamp with a very nasty smell | Gentle and quiet
test: In an older sense, what can noisome mean? | Happy and calm | *Harmful or very unpleasant | Very small and tiny | Musical and sweet
exam: Which word is a clue that noisome describes a horrible place in a story? | Lovely | *Dungeon | Bright | Sunny
